## Quick start guide

> **Assume you’ve already created a Bolt project and a Supabase project.**  
> If you haven’t, let me know and I’ll walk you through that first.

### 1. Enable Supabase Auth (email‑only)

```bash
# In the Supabase UI → Auth → Settings → General
# Set "Redirect URLs" to your Bolt app URL (e.g. https://app.bolt.com)
# Enable "Magic Link" (email) in "Logins and Signups"
```

### 2. Create the `messages` table

```sql
-- In Supabase → Database → SQL editor
create table messages (
  id uuid primary key default uuid_generate_v4(),
  sender_id text not null,
  recipient_id text not null,
  body text not null,
  sent_at timestamp default now()
);
```

### 3. Add RLS and policies

```sql
alter table messages enable row level security;

-- Anyone signed in can insert when they are the sender
create policy "insert own messages"
  on messages for insert
  using (auth.uid() = sender_id);

-- Anyone signed in can read a message if they are sender or recipient
create policy "select own messages"
  on messages for select
  using (auth.uid() in (sender_id, recipient_id));
```

### 4. Set up Bolt front‑end

> In Bolt, open the “Pages” tab, add a new page called `Messages`.

